{"id":"~Jing_Wang79","name":"Jing Wang","counts":{"accepted_papers":3,"first_position_papers":0,"co_first_author_papers":null,"corresponding_author_papers":null,"Oral":2,"Poster only":1},"papers":[{"id":"Bshs9HDDiu","title":"World Action Models are Zero-shot Policies","abstract":"State-of-the-art Vision-Language-Action (VLA) models excel at semantic generalization but struggle to generalize to unseen physical motions in novel environments. We introduce DreamZero, a World Action Model (WAM) built upon a pretrained video diffusion backbone. Unlike VLAs, WAMs learn physical dynamics by predicting future world states and actions, using video as a dense representation of how the world evolves. By jointly modeling video and action, DreamZero learns diverse skills effectively from heterogeneous robot data without relying on repetitive demonstrations. This results in over 2x improvement in generalization to new tasks in new environments compared to state-of-the-art VLAs in real-robot experiments. Crucially, through model and system optimizations, we enable a 14B autoregressive video diffusion model to perform real-time closed-loop control at 7Hz.","summary":"以联合预测未来视频与动作的 World Action Model 学习物理先验。DreamZero 研究多样化数据下的零样本任务泛化、跨构型视频迁移，以及新机器人上的少量数据适应。","type":"Oral","topics":["视觉语言动作与基础模型","模仿与示范学习","生成策略与扩散","安全、泛化与鲁棒性"],"title_topics":[],"authors":["~Seonghyeon_Ye1","~Yunhao_Ge1","~Kaiyuan_Zheng1","~Shenyuan_Gao1","~Sihyun_Yu2","~George_Kurian1","~Suneel_Indupuru1","~You_Liang_Tan1","~Chuning_Zhu1","~Jiannan_Xiang1","~Ayaan_Naveed_Malik1","~Kyungmin_Lee1","~William_Liang1","~Nadun_Ranawaka_Arachchige1","~Jiasheng_Gu1","~Yinzhen_Xu1","~Guanzhi_Wang1","~Fengyuan_Hu2","~Avnish_Narayan1","~Johan_Bjorck2","~Jing_Wang79","~Gwanghyun_Kim1","~Dantong_Niu1","~Ruijie_Zheng1","~Yuqi_Xie1","~Jimmy_Wu1","~Qi_Wang58","~Ryan_Julian2","~Danfei_Xu1","~Yilun_Du1","~Yevgen_Chebotar1","~Scott_Reed1","~Jan_Kautz1","~Yuke_Zhu1","~Linxi_Fan2","~Joel_Jang1"],"institutions":["NVIDIA"],"pdf":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2602.15922","openreview":"https://openreview.net/forum?id=Bshs9HDDiu","project":["https://dreamzero0.github.io"],"code":["https://github.com/dreamzero0/dreamzero"],"poster_date":"2026-11-09","poster_time":"5:00–6:30 PM","poster_venue":"JW Marriott","poster_number":51,"hardware":[{"model":"Agibot G1","env":["real"],"reviewed":false}],"has_social_sample":true,"role_evidence":{"cofirst":[],"corresponding":[],"project_lead":["Seonghyeon Ye","Yuke Zhu","Linxi Fan","Joel Jang"],"page":1,"note":"† Project Leads；* Core Contributors，均不等同共同一作或通讯。"},"author_role":{"id":"Bshs9HDDiu","position":21,"first":false,"roles":[]}},{"id":"WF4X17Al2r","title":"EgoScale: Scaling Dexterous Manipulation with Diverse Egocentric Human Data","abstract":"Human behavior is among the most scalable sources of data for learning physical intelligence, yet how to effectively leverage it for dexterous manipulation remains unclear. While prior work demonstrates human-to-robot transfer in constrained settings, it is unclear whether large-scale human data can support fine-grained, high-degree-of-freedom dexterous manipulation. We present EgoScale, a human-to-dexterous-manipulation transfer framework built on large-scale egocentric human data. We train a Vision–Language–Action (VLA) model on over 20,854 hours of action-labeled egocentric human video—more than 20× larger than prior efforts—and uncover a log-linear scaling law between human data scale and validation loss. This validation loss strongly correlates with downstream real-robot performance, establishing large-scale human data as a predictable supervision source. Beyond scale, we introduce a simple two-stage transfer recipe: large-scale human pretraining followed by lightweight aligned human–robot mid-training. This enables strong long-horizon dexterous manipulation and one-shot task adaptation with minimal robot supervision. Our final policy improves the average success rate by 54% over a no-pretraining baseline using a 22-DoF dexterous robotic hand, and transfers effectively to robots with lower-DoF hands, indicating that large-scale human motion provides a reusable, embodiment-agnostic motor prior.","summary":"用大规模第一人称人类操作视频预训练灵巧操作 VLA，再以轻量的人机对齐数据完成迁移。关注人类数据规模与真机表现的联系，以及低机器人数据条件下的长时任务和新手型适应。","type":"Oral","topics":["视觉语言动作与基础模型","灵巧操作与机器人手","记忆、推理与长时任务","人机交互与协作"],"title_topics":["灵巧操作与机器人手"],"authors":["~Ruijie_Zheng1","~Dantong_Niu1","~Yuqi_Xie1","~Jing_Wang79","~Mengda_Xu1","~Yunfan_Jiang1","~Fernando_Castañeda1","~Fengyuan_Hu2","~You_Liang_Tan1","~Letian_Fu1","~Trevor_Darrell2","~Furong_Huang1","~Yuke_Zhu1","~Danfei_Xu1","~Linxi_Fan2"],"institutions":["NVIDIA","University of California, Berkeley","University of Maryland"],"pdf":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2602.16710","openreview":"https://openreview.net/forum?id=WF4X17Al2r","project":[],"code":[],"poster_date":"2026-11-10","poster_time":"5:00–6:30 PM","poster_venue":"JW Marriott","poster_number":54,"hardware":[{"model":"Unitree G1","env":["real"],"reviewed":true},{"model":"Sharpa 灵巧手 / Wave","env":["real"],"reviewed":true},{"model":"Galaxea R1 / R1 Pro / R1 Lite","env":["real"],"reviewed":true},{"model":"OAK 相机","env":["real"],"reviewed":true}],"has_social_sample":true,"role_evidence":{"cofirst":["Ruijie Zheng","Dantong Niu","Yuqi Xie"],"project_lead":["Yuke Zhu","Danfei Xu","Linxi Fan"],"corresponding":[],"page":1,"note":"* Equal Contribution；† Project Lead。项目负责人不等同通讯作者。"},"author_role":{"id":"WF4X17Al2r","position":4,"first":false,"roles":[]}},{"id":"KdaClHHEUt","title":"T-Rex: Tactile-Reactive Dexterous Manipulation","abstract":"The ability to react dynamically to tactile signals has long been considered crucial to agile human-level dexterity. Yet contemporary learning-based VLAs for robotic manipulation generally either overlook the tactile modality or are limited to encoders with static cues, in part due to  the scarcity of diverse training data and standardized evaluation, architectural constraints in current Vision-Language-Action (VLA) models, and limitations of static tactile encoders. In this paper, we push the frontier of tactile-reactive manipulation addressing all of these limitations. We open-source a large-scale, 100-hour tactile-rich dataset collected via a novel, data-efficient recipe that prioritizes elementary motor primitives. To effectively exploit naturally high-frequency touch signals without sacrificing the existing capabilities of existing VLAs, we introduce a variable-rate Mix-of-Transformer (MoT) architecture equipped with a novel temporal tactile VQ-VAE encoder. We demonstrate the effectiveness of tactile-reactive policies on 12 manipulation tasks requiring delicate force control, deformable object manipulation, achieving over 30% higher average success rate than the strongest baseline.","summary":"围绕接触状态快速变化的灵巧操作，将触觉反馈用于反应式动作修正。研究多阶段训练如何帮助策略在手物接触中及时调整，而不只依赖视觉与预定动作。","type":"Poster only","topics":["视觉语言动作与基础模型","数据与评测","触觉与接触","灵巧操作与机器人手"],"title_topics":["触觉与接触","灵巧操作与机器人手"],"authors":["~Dantong_Niu1","~Zhuoyang_Liu1","~Zekai_Wang6","~Boning_Shao1","~Zhao-Heng_Yin1","~Anirudh_Pai1","~Yuvan_Sharma1","~Stefano_Saravalle1","~Ruijie_Zheng1","~Jing_Wang79","~Ryan_Punamiya1","~Mengda_Xu1","~Yuqi_Xie1","~Yunfan_Jiang1","~Letian_Fu1","~Konstantinos_Kallidromitis1","~Matteo_Gioia1","~Junyi_Zhang3","~Jiaxin_Ge1","~Haiwen_Feng1","~Fabio_Galasso1","~Wei_Zhan2","~David_M._Chan1","~Yutong_Bai1","~Roei_Herzig2","~Jiahui_Lei1","~Li_Fei-Fei1","~Ken_Goldberg1","~Jitendra_Malik2","~Pieter_Abbeel2","~Yuke_Zhu1","~Danfei_Xu1","~Linxi_Fan2","~Trevor_Darrell2"],"institutions":["ItalAI","NVIDIA","Panasonic","Sapienza University of Rome","Stanford University","University of California, Berkeley"],"pdf":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2606.17055","openreview":"https://openreview.net/forum?id=KdaClHHEUt","project":["https://tactile-rex.github.io","https://tactile-reactive-dexterous.github.io"],"code":["https://github.com/ZhuoyangLiu2005/T-Rex"],"poster_date":"2026-11-11","poster_time":"10:30 AM–12:00 PM","pos